// Azure: role assignment created or attempted (permissions granted)
// MITRE ATT&CK: Persistence / Privilege Escalation - T1098 Account Manipulation
// Granting a role is how access is given out in Azure - and how an attacker
// gives themselves or a backdoor identity more power.
// Failed attempts are included on purpose: someone TRYING to grant
// permissions they aren't allowed to grant is worth a look too.
//
// Late-arriving data: the Azure Activity log can reach Sentinel 5-15+ minutes
// after the event. The rule looks back 1 hour (query period) but only keeps
// rows that ARRIVED since the last 5-minute run, so each event alerts once,
// however late it lands. ("Start" rows are skipped: they're the same action.)
// Known benign in this lab: Terraform granting the shutdown Logic App its role.
AzureActivity
| where ingestion_time() > ago(5m)
| where OperationNameValue =~ "MICROSOFT.AUTHORIZATION/ROLEASSIGNMENTS/WRITE"
| where ActivityStatusValue in ("Success", "Failure")
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, CallerIpAddress, ActivityStatusValue,
          ResourceGroup, Scope = _ResourceId, CorrelationId
